  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "The records strongly establish computational control or characterization of chemical SRO in closely related BCC refractory HEAs, including Monte Carlo/first-principles predictions of temperature-dependent ordering, clustering, and precipitates. Other records establish B2/BCC ordering in HEAs. Thus, simulating different SRO states in HfNbTaTiZr would be a plausible proposal. However, none connects SRO to increased lattice thermal conductivity through reduced lattice distortion, percolating high-conductivity cluster pathways, or modified high-frequency phonon density of states. Reconstructing that transport mechanism and the predicted conductivity enhancement would require a substantial additional idea."
